class:: StereoCorrelation
summary:: Rolling Pearson correlation of two audio channels
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Amplitude

description::
Subtracts each channel mean over the exact rolling sample window, then divides covariance by the square root of the product of the channel variances. Constant or silent channels return zero.

Uses an exact rolling sample window, with output held at zero until it is full. The update cost is linear in the input block size, with a once-per-window sum rebase to bound roundoff drift. Memory is two windows of doubles, allocated at initialization. Formulas are independently implemented from energy, M/S decomposition, and Pearson correlation. Silence returns zero.

Vanilla Amplitude can track channel levels separately; this UGen directly relates the channels over a fixed shared interval.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: left
Left audio-rate input.

argument:: right
Right audio-rate input.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time rolling window, 0.001..2 seconds; default 0.05.

returns::
Correlation from -1 through +1.

examples::
StereoCorrelation measures the rolling Pearson correlation coefficient between left and right audio channels (-1 for inverted/out-of-phase audio, 0 for uncorrelated stereo, +1 for identical mono). In this example, when correlation drops below zero (out-of-phase danger), an adaptive phase guard smoothly collapses low-frequency bass to mono, preventing acoustic phase cancellation on playback. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.stereo:: displays the stereo correlation readout.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("stereo.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 3);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.isKindOf(Buffer) and: { ~mir2Buffer.numChannels >= 2 }) {
            PlayBuf.ar(2, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
                var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
                [sig, DelayC.ar(sig, 0.02, 0.003)]
            } {
                // Synthetic stereo fallback
                var l = Saw.ar(220) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                var r = Saw.ar(222) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                [l, r]
            }
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]);

        var corr = StereoCorrelation.kr(source[0], source[1], windowTime: 0.05);
        var corrLag = corr.lag(0.08);
        var monoCollapse = (corrLag < 0.2).lag(0.02, 0.1);
        var lowBassMono = (LPF.ar(source[0], 200) + LPF.ar(source[1], 200)) * 0.5;
        var outL = (source[0] * (1 - (monoCollapse * 0.6))) + (lowBassMono * monoCollapse * 0.6);
        var outR = (source[1] * (1 - (monoCollapse * 0.6))) + (lowBassMono * monoCollapse * 0.6);
        var sound = [outL, outR] * 0.25;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, [0.0, 1.0, corrLag]) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.stereo("Stereo Correlation", ~mir2Bus);
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

